'''Turanian''' (tū-rā′ni-an), ''a.'' and ''n.'' [< ''Turan'' (see ''Iranian'') + ''-ian''.] A word loosely and indefinitely used to designate a family of languages, sometimes applied to the Asiatic languages in general outside of the Indo-European and Semitic families, and so including various discordant and independent families, but sometimes used especially or restrictedly of the Ural-Altaic or Scythian family.

